"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518839,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg4Mzk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"ffddff","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-08-05T13:39:33Z","updated_at":"2025-10-09T12:16:56Z","closed_at":"2025-10-09T12:15:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109335","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109335","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109335.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109335.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Recently I noticed that someone in our community misunderstood these methods / property as being related to resource UID. After checking the documentation and source code, I found that the descriptions are not accurate.\r\n\r\nIn this PR:\r\n- Improved the descriptions: These concepts are not necessarily related to scenes. They are the unique IDs of the `ext_resource` and `subresource` tags in tres / tscn files.\r\n- The string returned by `generate_scene_unique_id()` is neither guaranteed to be unique nor is it an identifier itself. The engine only uses this function to generate part of an identifier.\r\n- Currently, the terms \"subresource\" and \"built-in\" are both used in the APIs to describe \"nested resources\". So I added relevant explanations in the class descriptions.","closed_by":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/fol